note bottom of CoEvolutionTrainer
  Registered as "coevolution". Three modes:
  competitive_2pop, self_play_hof, cooperative.
  Schedule: synchronous | alternating.
  Reports reporting_side's best policy.
  train() is a slim orchestrator: validate ->
  _initialize_sides -> with executor: bootstrap
  -> _run_synchronous_loop | _run_alternating_loop
  -> persist. _step_one_side is the shared per-side
  body for both schedules (review S1).
  Honors budget_on_consumed=True (ENV_STEPS): stops when
  the summed per-side real env ticks reach budget_value
  (shared aggregate pool; finish-generation-then-stop).
  budget_split="per_side" (requires budget_on_consumed)
  grants each evolving side budget/n slice instead;
  on_side_exhausted: "freeze" = exhausted side stops
  evolving but keeps serving its pool (run ends when all
  slices spent) | "cutoff" = whole run stops at the first
  exhausted side (pool under-spent).
end note
}

